From cf0648ed2f8c7ecc6864f0b097f2d6aad361aeb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:42:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(approval): review sees job ids; own jobs need no card

The provenance review dropped every call's task_id and session_id
arguments, so a process_manage kill read as naming no process, and
neither the judge nor the approval card could tie it to the agent's own
background job.

The review now sees every argument. A kill, stop, steer or stdin write
of a background process or subagent that this agent or one of its own
subagents started this session runs without a card: the harness checks
it against the process registry (owners, including processes a
subagent handed off or left to its parent) and its own records in the
transcript (the session_id and pid a background terminal call
returned, the subagents and handed-off processes a delegate_task call
returned). This covers terminal `kill <pid>` of those PIDs. Any other
target is reviewed as before, with a harness fact saying it is not one
of the agent's jobs.

delegation.keep_child_processes no longer hands the parent pure wait
loops (`while pgrep -f ...; do sleep N; done`), which watched the
child's own work and often never end: they stop with the child and are
listed as stopped_wait_loops. Kept processes carry a `what` (a build, a
test run, a server, ...) in their record and handoff note.
